Suppose a fixed original derivative of \(F\) is bounded by its actual parameter factor times \(\zeta(X)\delta(X)^{-M}\); the parameter factor is constant during the radial integration and may contain the original \(q\), \(\varepsilon\), \(S_*\) and logarithmic powers. Apply (R47), (R50), and the bounded radial factors to the left representation (R51) or right representation (R52). On either edge, the integral is bounded by that same parameter factor times a fixed constant and \(\zeta(X)\delta(X)^{3-M}\), with the explicit additional \(\sqrt{q/2}\) from (R51)--(R52). For example, the left-edge constant can be taken as \[
